WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.323
^- Are you encouraged to fight with your costars?

00:00:12.766 --> 00:00:13.763
^Uh... yeah.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.960
That's like the whole point of reality TV.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.720
- They definitely put you in situations where

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.070
there's likely to be drama,

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.230
they'll put you in a smaller group setting

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.793
to allow that to happen naturally.

00:00:23.793 --> 00:00:27.342
- We fought off camera, and we let the producers know

00:00:27.342 --> 00:00:30.260
and they wanted us to repeat that fight on-camera,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.780
which only increased the intensity of it

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.640
because neither of us wanted to do it.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.200
- We're definitely not encouraged to fight.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.640
Add drinking to the mix, not knowing each other,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.500
having no cell phones, no TV,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.333
we're gonna get on each other's nerves a little bit.

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.920
- The other person on the show with me

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.060
was told to start some things with me

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.960
because they felt like I was going to, you know, bring it.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.883
Which I did, but it was still me.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.660
^- Do you or other people on your show

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.360
^turn up personalities for the camera?

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.280
Yes, they do, they'll be lying if they say otherwise.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.270
I think everyone knows where and when the cameras are on.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.000
Including myself, I'm guilty.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.223
You can't be like, hi.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.323
My name's Joe.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.030
Who the heck would want to watch that?

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.590
You always got to turn it up.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.204
You don't turn up, you're not getting airtime,

00:01:14.204 --> 00:01:15.702
you're going to be edited out of the show

00:01:15.702 --> 00:01:17.493
or barely be in the show.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.070
- Our personalities are real.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.090
We didn't turn it up for the cameras.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.410
We got casted because of our crazy ridiculous personalities

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.483
and it's just us.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.620
^- Do you get paid to be on a reality show?

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.480
Uh... yeah!

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.753
- We do get a stipend.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.050
I'm not gonna go travel the world with a stipend, so...

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.080
- It wasn't much.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.190
- As the seasons go on you typically get paid more

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.731
because you negotiate your contracts,

00:01:40.731 --> 00:01:42.673
but we got paid per episode.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.823
^- Everyone makes about ten grand.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.920
^It grows from about like 2,500 dollars I think per episode

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.270
^and it's kind of like Who Wants to Be a Millionaire,

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.093
^so as you get closer to first,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.470
it's like, I think, a hundred and fifty thousand dollars,

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.260
fifty thousand for second, third,

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.023
and then it kind of goes down.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.290
^- Do you feel like you have to do your hair and makeup

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.660
^perfectly every day because you're always on camera?

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.860
- I did feel like I always had to do my makeup and I always

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.750
had to have my hair done, which was quite expensive.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.100
- I mean you want to look the best that you can on camera.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.600
- I actually dread doing it.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.180
I have to coach myself through it.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.080
I had my female roommates helping me and that

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.930
was a little bit nice because I didn't have to do it myself.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.393
- Come on, makeup?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.920
The hair, yeah.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.570
Gotta be groomed nice, you gotta work out.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.610
Always gotta look fresh.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.683
If you're not fresh, don't even be on TV.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:35.693
- I Would try to keep up every day with the old man bun.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.600
And then the hair, you gotta look good on camera.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.590
We only get one outfit for the entire time

00:02:40.638 --> 00:02:42.607
that we're out there, so,

00:02:42.607 --> 00:02:45.940
hopefully you're wearing something that you enjoy wearing

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.940
because it is a long thirty-nine days.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.373
^- Do I ever watch my show?

00:02:50.785 --> 00:02:53.890
^Yeah I mean I watched it at the time.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.690
It's hard to watch me on camera,

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.090
but normally I don't like to watch myself on TV.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.203
- Of course I watch my show!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.881
Not only do I watch my show, I have episode release parties

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:05.013
with my friends from my show.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.520
- Come on, I'm not gonna be there for two months or a month

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.280
whatever it may be and not watch my show.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.693
- I watched it when it was airing and then I live-tweeted,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.570
but after that, I mean, I'm not reliving my glory days

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.090
and watching it every night before I go to sleep.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.280
- I did watch it and quite frankly I don't need

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.990
to watch it again, once was enough.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.200
I mean, your voice sounds really annoying all the time.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.130
- Absolutely I watch my show.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.153
Nothing else beats Survivor, nothing.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.900
^Do you ever get used to a camera

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.320
^following you everywhere?

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.810
I would say after about a week or so

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.852
you kind of forget that they're always around.

00:03:35.852 --> 00:03:38.348
- At first, couldn't get used to it.

00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:40.881
In the first couple of days I'm like oh my God,

00:03:40.881 --> 00:03:44.521
I woke up, I looked at Carissa next to me, my castmate,

00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:47.680
and I was like aaah, there's a camera in my face!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.793
- At the beginning, it was insane.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.213
I was self-conscious, oh my God.

00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:54.083
- When I was in Dating Naked though, that was weird.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:54.923
Because I'm naked!

00:03:54.923 --> 00:03:57.863
And to have someone right there on you, like hey,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.063
looking at your naked parts, no no no!

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.292
But actually, in the end, I kind of

00:04:02.292 --> 00:04:05.670
got used to it a little bit, so I go ahead

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.850
and starting acting my personality like ten times higher.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.060
- I had never been in front of the camera before like that.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.410
I had never been on TV before, not into acting,

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:13.313
none of that kind of stuff.

00:04:13.313 --> 00:04:16.204
But after three or four times and a few drinks,

00:04:16.204 --> 00:04:17.849
things get a little easier.

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:21.230
^- Does the publicity ever affect you negatively - yes!

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.684
Oh my god, people would use you.

00:04:22.684 --> 00:04:24.770
Hey Joe, you got any hookups for TV?

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.753
Yes, I do have hookups, but guess what?

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.593
You're not getting them.

00:04:27.593 --> 00:04:29.443
Don't just ask me to hang out with me for that.

00:04:29.443 --> 00:04:33.050
- People are always going to have their opinions about you

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:36.542
regardless, so, you just have to be grounded

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.830
within yourself and not let people's words get to you.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.720
- I thought that I was just going to cry

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.740
when I would read Twitter and social media.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.060
I read these comments that people write to me at times and

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.524
you can't help but laugh and just brush it under the rug.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:55.490
What is the best perk about being a reality TV star?

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.662
- Getting free stuff and getting paid to go places.

00:04:57.662 --> 00:05:00.312
- Obviously all the dick pics that I've been getting.

00:05:01.011 --> 00:05:02.812
- I am a social worker first,

00:05:02.812 --> 00:05:06.770
and I get to talk about what I do and what I love,

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.529
social services with foster children,

00:05:08.529 --> 00:05:11.020
I get to tell the masses about it.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.253
- I'm able to give back to my community,

00:05:13.374 --> 00:05:16.380
and try to promote some healthy healing

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.800
and anything I can do to help.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.550
It was fun, it's been an amazing experience thus far.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.200
Wouldn't change it for the world.

